       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I know you're the clinician and that you're taking responsibility for it. But 50 mg daily is five times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any indication where that dose is appropriate or safe. The risks are serious hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and they would fall on the patient. Documenting the decision in the chart wouldn't reduce that risk.\n\nHere are some ways to go forward:\n- **If the goal is more blood pressure control:** I can enter 10 mg once daily, the maximum dose. You could also add or adjust a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. I can enter those orders if you tell me which.\n- **If you think this dose is truly needed:** Please talk with pharmacy or a clinical pharmacologist first. A pharmacist-reviewed override would be a safer route than my entering it directly.\n- **If this was a typo:** Tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away."
